course: dictionary
lesson: 13330
title: A book that guides you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A guidebook is a book that gives information to visitors about a place. «We took a guidebook to the museum so we would know where to go.» The word has two parts: guide, which means show the way, and book. A guidebook is a book that guides you.
explain: Guidebooks often have maps, history and tips. «The guidebook said the castle was built about 800 years ago.» The sentence tells you what a guidebook contains, so you can work out its meaning from the words around it.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Dad read the guidebook on the train» still makes sense if you think of a guidebook as a book about a place. Guidebook is a noun: one is a guidebook, and several are guidebooks.
fact: A guidebook is a book that gives information to visitors about a place.
fact: A guidebook can be about a city, a country, a museum or a castle.
fact: Guidebooks often include maps, history and tips.
fact: «According to the guidebook» means "as the guidebook says".
fact: In stories, a guidebook can help travellers find hidden places.
exercise: «We took a guidebook to the museum so we would know where to go.» What is a guidebook? | *A book that gives information to visitors about a place | A kind of school book | A ticket to get into a museum | A map that you can fold up and put in your pocket
exercise: Mum says, «According to the guidebook, the castle is very old.» What does according to the guidebook mean? | *As the guidebook says | Before the guidebook was written | Without reading the guidebook at all | Because the guidebook is broken
exercise: In «Dad read the guidebook on the train», which word names the book? | *guidebook | Dad | read | train
test: What is a guidebook for? | To cook dinner for a family | To sell cars at the market | *To give visitors information about a place
test: In «The guidebook has maps, history and tips», what is inside the guidebook? | Jokes and songs | Recipes and shopping lists | Football scores | *Maps, history and tips
exam: Jayden writes, «My class will write a guidebook for our town.» What is the class making? | *A book giving information about the town | A new school | A map of the moon | A cake recipe
